1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:12,269
Welcome. From today, the Wits AHEAD website speaks eleven languages. Here is what is new, and how you can share it with the people around you.

2
00:00:13,669 --> 00:00:41,250
Every page now has a globe at the top. Tap it, and you see eleven languages in two groups. The global languages: English, French, Spanish, Portuguese, Chinese and Arabic. And the African languages: Kiswahili, isiZulu, Yoruba, Hausa and Naija. Your choice is remembered, so the site opens in your language next time.

3
00:00:42,649 --> 00:01:00,280
Everything is translated: the daily briefing, the research cases from our projects, and the researcher profiles. Eight editions can also be heard. Each morning the briefing is read aloud, and that now includes Kiswahili and Arabic.

4
00:01:01,679 --> 00:01:09,619
Karibuni. Sasa mnaweza kusoma na kusikiliza taarifa ya Wits AHEAD kwa Kiswahili, kila asubuhi.

5
00:01:11,019 --> 00:01:20,789
أهلًا وسهلًا. يمكنكم الآن قراءة موجز Wits AHEAD والاستماع إليه باللغة العربية، كل صباح.

6
00:01:22,189 --> 00:01:34,889
Hausa, Yoruba and Naija are written editions for now, because no natural voice for them exists yet. Every research case and every profile is there, in each of them.

7
00:01:36,289 --> 00:01:57,029
Now, please share it. Send the website to your friends, your family and your colleagues, in the language they read best. Each language has its own address: witsahead dot org, slash, and then the language, such as s w for Kiswahili, or z u for isiZulu.

8
00:01:58,429 --> 00:02:09,399
The work of this group, yours included, can now be read across Africa and beyond, in the languages people think in. Thank you for sharing it.
